From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:28:41 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] internal/syscall/windows: replace a rename target where POSIX rename is missing

Root.Rename (CL 659416, commit 2ffda87, Go 1.25) asks for a rename that
replaces whatever the destination holds. Windows 7, 8 and 8.1 do not have
that rename, some early versions of Windows 10 refuse it onto a link, and
the older rename refuses to replace a link to a directory or a file another
program has open.

Let such a rename replace the destination there too. Move the destination
aside, rename, then delete the moved copy.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7, 8, 8.1,     renaming onto a        the destination is
	some early Windows 10  directory link or an   replaced
	                       open file fails
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 10 22H2, 11,   the destination is     the destination is
	on NTFS                replaced               replaced

Gate: version, then query (Windows 10 before 22H2) | Remembered: Y

